== R1 a query parameter's type is enforced only when its body cannot bind it
   Query bright(t: thing) means lit(t).   facts lit(lamp), lit(hall: place)
   bright(?t)             -> hall,lamp   (hall is a place, not a thing)
   test bright(hall)      -> true
   Query dark(t: thing) means not lit(t).
   dark(?t)               -> cup   (ranged over things only)
   dark(?x) and at(?x, hall) vs at(?x, hall) and dark(?x): cup / cup
   with at(yard: place, hall): dark(?x) -> cup;  at(?x, hall) and dark(?x) -> cup,yard
   (adding a conjunct yields an answer the query alone denies: yard is no thing)

== R2 a count taken past nothing: a rule clamps it, an action's admits refuses it
   Decrease gold(ann) by 5        apply -> gold 0    admits -> false
   Increase gold(ann) by 0 - 5    apply -> gold 0    admits -> false
   Set gold(ann) to 0 - 5         apply -> gold -5   admits -> false
   Set gold(ann) to 1 - 5 + 4     apply -> gold 0    admits -> true
   [-5, +5] apply -> 5; [+5, -5] apply -> 3  (net change 0 both ways)

== R3 dice in arithmetic
   dice(cup)=21 dice(jar)=18 dice(cup)+dice(cup)=42  (one die per thing per watch)
   Increase count(cup) by dice(cup): apply -> 21
   count(cup)=5; Decrease count(cup) by dice(cup): admits -> true (admits reads the die as a stored measure, 0), apply -> 0

== R4 the idle-rule cache does not see entities added to the world (withModule keeps the line)
   before: instances = 0 (no things yet; the rule is now remembered idle)
   a thing cup joins (as an installation/frontier adds entities): test unmarked(cup) and not lit(cup) = true
   same rule object: instances = 0;  fresh rule object: 1
